§ T28 EMIT-FRAMEWORK (~450 LOC)
  Emit_Target enum : MIR Markdown HTML LaTeX JSON
  Emit_Config : source_map + sign + incremental + standalone + schema_print
  Emit_Context : source_file + source_text + ast_root + tc_result + ir_module
  emit(ctx) → Emit_Result { bytes + source_map + cert + schema_version }
  cache lookup/store pre/post emission
  cert via smt_audit Ed25519 reusable ; canonical = target|schema|hash(body)

§ T28.5 JSON BACKEND (210 LOC)
  unified superset : {schema, schemaVersion, source, ast, types, ir}
  source-block : {file, bytes, sha256}
  ast-block : recursive {kind, text, pos{line,col,byte}, suffix?, children[]}
  types-block : {refine_obligations, strict_parse, diagnostics[]}
  ir-block    : reuses ir_json.ir_json_module
  schema : emit_schema/json-v1.schema ; draft 2020-12

§ T28.2 MARKDOWN BACKEND (135 LOC)
  <!-- schema: markdown-v1 --> header
  <!-- source: <path> --> provenance
  # <derived-title> from filename stem
  § Name → ## Name + <a id="anchor"> for cross-ref
  definitions rendered as fenced ```csl blocks via pprint reconstruction
  comments → blockquotes (> text)
  consumers : Jekyll/Hugo/Docusaurus/Astro/GitHub-browser/pandoc

§ T28.3 HTML BACKEND (230 LOC)
  standalone HTML5 ; fragment mode available
  CSS taxonomy : 12 CSS variables + per-token-kind classes
  TOC sidebar : sticky nav collecting all §-headings
  inline highlighter : hand-rolled char-walk emitting <span class="csl-*">
  12 category classes : section/glyph/operator/evidence/number/keyword/
                         morpheme/modal/string/number/type/comment
  schema : emit_schema/html-v1.css

§ T28.4 LATEX BACKEND (170 LOC)
  article-class standalone ; cslv3.sty style-package
  listings-language=csl with 30+ literate rewrites for glyphs
  unicode-math + xunicode + xltxtra for XeLaTeX/LuaLaTeX compile
  morpheme → \cslmorph{tag} (\textsubscript styled)
  modal → \cslmodal{text}
  cross-refs → \cslref{label}{text}
  experimental : requires latexmk to compile ; not blocking v1.0
  schema : emit_schema/latex-v1.sty

§ T28.1 MIR BACKEND (220 LOC)
  CSSLv3-MIR textual ; MLIR-flavor w/ cssl.* dialect
  cslv3_to_cssl mapping : 40+ ops explicitly mapped
    cslv3.fn → cssl.fn ; cslv3.add → cssl.arith.add ; etc.
    prefix-swap fallback for unknown cslv3.* ops
  attr preservation : morpheme + sig + value + name + kind ALL carried
  region + block layout identical to parser.ir_print ; only op-names rewritten
  schema : emit_schema/mir-v1.json ; json-schema draft 2020-12
  opMapping table exposed in schema for consumer validation

§ T28 SOURCE-MAP infrastructure (120 LOC)
  v3 sourcemap JSON skeleton (non-VLQ per-segment for simplicity)
  Source_Map_Builder : sources[] + names[] + segments[]
  smb_record(gen_line, gen_col, orig_line, orig_col, name?)
  default : one-segment-per-AST-node fallback from emit_context
  sidecar .map files written on --out=<path> with --source-map

§ T28 EMIT-CACHE (180 LOC)
  location : .emit-cache/<hash[:2]>/<hash[2:]>.json
  key : BLAKE2B(source_text | target | schema_version | config_hash)
  entry : {bytes + source_map + cert + target + schema_version + created_ms}
  serialize : hand-roll JSON w/ escape-aware string writer
  parse : extract_json_string w/ unescape (fixed during Session-10)
  LRU-eviction : deferred to Session-11 (soft-cap 50MB documented)

§ T28 CLI
  --emit=<target>        mir|markdown|html|latex|json
  --out=<path>           write to file ; .map + .cert sidecars
  --sign                 Ed25519-sign via smt_audit chain
  --incremental          consult .emit-cache ; skip-re-emit
  --fragment             (HTML/LaTeX) omit <html>/<head> + \documentclass
  --no-source-map        disable .map sidecar
  --schema               print target schema and exit
  parser --emit-selftest 5 programmatic targets ; sample "§ T\n  hp : i32"

